    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.k_shell - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.k_shell.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.k_shell()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Extract the k-shell subgraph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.k_shell()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Extract the k-shell subgraph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.k_shell()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Extract the k-shell subgraph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nExtract the k-shell subgraph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L58230-L58325){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.k_shell(k)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![k-shell](../assets/graphs/k-shell.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Left: the eight-node graph with a dense cluster A to D, a ring E, F, G and a pendant H. Right: the 2-shell holds the nodes whose coreness is exactly 2, so E, F, G and the edges E to F and F to G are in the accent color, while the 3-core A to D and the pendant H (coreness 1) are dashed.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nThe k-shell contains nodes with coreness exactly equal to `k`. The coreness of a node is the\nhighest `k` for which the node is part of the k-core.\n\nEquivalently, the k-shell is the k-core minus the `(k+1)`-core: the layer of nodes that\nis peeled away when going from one core to the next. The shells partition the graph, so\nevery node belongs to exactly one of them. This \"onion\" view of a network is useful for:\n\n- locating nodes by how deep they sit, from the periphery (low `k`) to the core (high\n  `k`)\n- studying a single layer, for example the nodes that are fairly well connected but not\n  part of the innermost core\n- comparing how the layers are populated across networks\n\nThe returned graph contains only the shell's nodes and the edges *between* them; edges\nthat connect the shell to other shells are dropped, so the result can be sparse or even\nedgeless. To get every node's coreness at once, use `coreness()`; see also `k_core()`\nand `k_crust()`.\n\nDegrees count edges without weights. For directed graphs, degree means out-degree. The\noriginal graph is not modified. The returned graph keeps the node and edge IDs, labels,\nweights and attributes of the original.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[k]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Coreness value to extract. Must be a non-negative integer. `k=0` gives the isolated\n    nodes. If no node has coreness exactly `k`, the result is an empty graph.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   New graph containing only the k-shell nodes and their connecting edges.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~coreness`) \n\n:   The coreness of every node.\n\n[](`~k_core`) \n\n:   The nodes with coreness at least `k`.\n\n[](`~k_corona`) \n\n:   The nodes of the shell with exactly `k` neighbors in the core.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nThis graph has a dense cluster `A`-`D`, a loop through `E`, `F` and `G`, and a pendant\nnode `H`. Its three shells split the nodes into the pendant (coreness 1), the loop\n(coreness 2) and the cluster (coreness 3):\n\n::: {#b19fd0ab .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"A\", \"C\"), (\"A\", \"D\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"B\", \"D\"),\n     (\"C\", \"D\"), (\"C\", \"E\"), (\"D\", \"E\"), (\"E\", \"F\"), (\"F\", \"G\"),\n     (\"G\", \"D\"), (\"G\", \"H\")]\n)\n\n{\n    k: sorted(graph.k_shell(k).get_node_df()[\"label\"].to_list())\n    for k in [1, 2, 3]\n}\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n{1: ['H'], 2: ['E', 'F', 'G'], 3: ['A', 'B', 'C', 'D']}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nOnly the edges inside a shell are kept. The 2-shell keeps `E`-`F` and `F`-`G`, but not\nthe edges from `E` and `G` into the cluster:\n\n::: {#5a3000f7 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ngraph.k_shell(2).count_edges()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n2\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### One layer out from the barricade\n\n`les_miserables()` links two characters of Victor Hugo's novel when they appear in the\nsame chapter. The innermost core is the twelve characters at the barricade, with\ncoreness 9. The next shell holds Valjean and Javert, the Thenardiers' daughter Eponine,\nand Thenardier with four members of the gang:\n\n::: {#6befb24f .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nnovel = ec.les_miserables()\nshell = novel.k_shell(8)\n\nsorted(shell.get_node_df()[\"label\"].to_list())\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n['Babet',\n 'Claquesous',\n 'Eponine',\n 'Gueulemer',\n 'Javert',\n 'Montparnasse',\n 'Thenardier',\n 'Valjean']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#843de703 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nshell.plot(label_by=\"label\", seed=1)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"5.5 13.9 689.0 492.1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"5.5\" y=\"13.9\"